# Project Conventions

## Confirm before changing files (G3)
List every create/modify/delete and **wait for confirmation**. See `.cursor/rules/confirm-before-edit.mdc`.

## Conventional Commits (S9)
`hook-commit-guard` blocks non-conforming messages (`feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, `refactor:`, `test:`, `docs:`, `style:`, `perf:`, `build:`, `ci:`, `revert:`).

## No `console.log` in Production Code (S10)
Do not leave `console.log` / `warn` / `error` in production-bound code. Use a Nest logger.

## No Hardcoded Secrets (H6)
Never hardcode secrets. Use `ConfigService` and `.env.example` (no real values). `hook-secret-scan` blocks secret patterns in writes.

## Package Install Approval (H7)
`npm install` (no args) is allowed. `npm install <package>` requires user approval.

## Automated Hooks (G2)
Do not bypass hooks.

| Event | Hook |
|----|---|
| `preToolUse` | `hook-protect-env`, `hook-secret-scan` |
| `afterFileEdit` | `hook-format-and-lint` (oxlint + prettier) |
| `beforeShellExecution` | `hook-commit-guard`, `hook-branch-guard`, `hook-dep-install` |
| `stop` | `hook-readme-sync` |
